{{also|unilatéral}}
==English==

===Etymology===
A modern creation (c. 1802), from {{der|en|NL.|unilateralis|t=one-sidely, one-sided}}, from {{der|en|la|ūnus|t=one}} + {{m|la|laterālis|t=sided, lateral}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Done by one [[side]] only.
# Affecting only one side of the body.
# Binding or affecting one party only.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|onesidedly}}
* {{l|en|one-sidely}}

